# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub rejects any push containing a single file larger than 100 MB.
# Everything listed here is real project content that lives on disk only and
# travels between machines inside the Drive content zips.
# Never `git add` these. If one ever needs to be versioned, shrink it first
# (or set up Git LFS, which this repo does not use).
#
# T_m_nrw_blazer_BN.uasset is a 222 MB crowd normal map -- it was purged from
# history on 2026-09-18 because it blocked the first push. See the Brain note
# "Battle of ATL" for the full story.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content/CitySampleCrowd/Character/Male/NormalWeight/Textures/blazer/T_m_nrw_blazer_BN.uasset
Content/EuropeanHornbeam/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The review maps. One per review harness, about 70 MB each, and they belong in
# the Drive content zips with the rest of the heavy content - Windows said so
# themselves ("they travel in the content zip, not the repo, because of GitHub's
# file limits").
#
# On 2026-09-19 a `git add -A` while merging Windows round 15 put 39 of them,
# 2.65 GB, into this repo and pushed it. This rule is so that cannot happen
# again by accident; `git add -f` still overrides it if a map is ever wanted in
# git on purpose (PiedmontCarLaneReview was asked for that way once).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Content/PiedmontRide/Maps/*Review.umap
Content/PiedmontRide/Maps/ScooterPreservationBackup.umap

Build/
work/
Scripts/last-seen-release.txt
